    "title": "States Take Action Against Potential Voter Intimidation by Federal Immigration Officers",
    "text": "•\tDemocratic-led states are taking steps to counter potential voter intimidation by federal immigration officers during the midterm elections.\n•\tStates are concerned about federal immigration officers patrolling polling places.\n•\tThe ACLU and other groups are also monitoring the situation.\n•\tNew Mexico's Attorney General has issued a legal opinion stating that federal agents cannot access polling places.\n•\tOther states are also taking action, including California and New York.\n•\tThe actions include training poll workers and informing voters of their rights.\n•\tSome states are considering legislation to further protect voters.\n•\tThe goal is to ensure that voters feel safe and are not intimidated at the polls.\n•\tThe article also mentions concerns about potential challenges to election results.",
